Campfire wasm patch 0102: let the app start a NEW wallet without scanning history.

WasmWalletClient::StartWallet always called enableBodyRequests(true), so every
wallet on a public node downloaded and scanned every block body since genesis
(about 4.07 M blocks, measured ~1,050 blocks/s in Chrome: over an hour) unless
BEAM's 330 MB recovery snapshot was imported first. A freshly generated seed
has nothing to find in the past, and regular (SBBS) payments confirm their own
outputs through UTXO proofs, so the desktop wallet-api runs such wallets with
body requests off (--request_bodies defaults to false).

Adds setBodyRequests(bool) (JS: client.setBodyRequests(false) before
startWallet()). The default stays true, so restore and existing callers behave
exactly as upstream. What a wallet without scanning cannot see: payments to
offline / max-privacy / public addresses (create_address refuses those types
with "Wallet must be connected to own node or mobile node protocol should be
turned on"), and coins received or spent by another copy of the same seed.
Importing the recovery snapshot later (with body requests on) brings all of
that back.

--- a/wasmclient/wasmclient.cpp
+++ b/wasmclient/wasmclient.cpp
@@ -482,6 +482,19 @@
         m_ApproveContractInfoHandler = std::make_unique<val>(std::move(handler));
     }
 
+    // Campfire: block-body scanning ("mobile node") is what lets a wallet on a
+    // public node find coins it did not negotiate itself: a restored seed's
+    // history, offline / max-privacy receipts, coins moved by another copy of
+    // the seed. A freshly generated seed has no history, and regular (SBBS)
+    // payments are confirmed through their own UTXO proofs, so for a new
+    // wallet the app can switch scanning off (as wallet-api does by default)
+    // instead of reading every block since genesis. Call before startWallet().
+    void SetBodyRequests(bool enable)
+    {
+        AssertMainThread();
+        m_BodyRequests = enable;
+    }
+
     void ExecuteAPIRequest(const std::string& request)
     {
         AssertMainThread();
@@ -554,7 +567,7 @@
             {
                 m_Client->getAsync()->importRecovery(std::move(m_CurrentRecoveryFile)); // m_CurrentRecoveryFile should be cleared 
             }
-            m_Client->getAsync()->enableBodyRequests(true);
+            m_Client->getAsync()->enableBodyRequests(m_BodyRequests); // Campfire: was always true
             m_Client->start({}, true, additionalTxCreators);
         }
         catch (const std::exception& ex)
@@ -1025,6 +1038,7 @@
     WalletClient2::Ptr m_Client;
     IWalletApi::Ptr m_WalletApi;
     bool m_Headless = false;
+    bool m_BodyRequests = true; // Campfire: upstream behaviour unless the app opts out
     std::string m_CurrentRecoveryFile;
 };
 
@@ -1055,6 +1069,7 @@
         .function("setSyncHandler", &WasmWalletClient::SetSyncHandler)
         .function("setApproveSendHandler", &WasmWalletClient::SetApproveSendHandler)
         .function("setApproveContractInfoHandler", &WasmWalletClient::SetApproveContractInfoHandler)
+        .function("setBodyRequests", &WasmWalletClient::SetBodyRequests)
         .function("createAppAPI", &WasmWalletClient::CreateAppAPI)
         .function("createAppAPI", &WasmWalletClient::CreateAppAPI2)
         .function("createAppAPI", &WasmWalletClient::CreateAppAPI3)
